  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive nucleus decays by two different process. The half life of the first process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> minutes and that of the second process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The effective half-life of the nucleus is calculated to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "300",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Decay law for both process can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, net decay will become</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mi>N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>30</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, required value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}